**user**:
> I got a message from a new friend on facebook, who was going to find some armor for me: "Hey just in case you didn't see I tagged in in a bunch of possibilities... two full kits". But where would I find this in facebook?
**assistant**:
> To find the posts where you've been tagged, you should:
> 
> 1. **Go to your Facebook Notifications**: Click on the bell icon at the top right of the Facebook interface. This will show you recent activity related to your profile, including tags.
> 
> 2. **Check Your Activity Log**: 
>    - Click on your profile picture in the top right to go to your profile page.
>    - Click on the three dots (`...`) next to the "Edit profile" button.
>    - Select "Activity log."
>    - In the activity log, you can filter the list by "Posts You're Tagged In" to find posts or comments in which you've been tagged.
> 
> 3. **Check Your Timeline Review** (if applicable):
>    - If you have timeline review enabled, tagged posts might wait for your approval before appearing on your timeline. Go to Settings & Privacy > Settings > Profile and Tagging, and make sure that you check posts in this queue.
> 
> By following these steps, you should be able to review the posts where your friend has tagged you for those armor possibilities. If you're still having trouble, you might want to ask your friend to share the links directly with you via message.
